fuse_setcc_branch (Agent Z, #274) audit follow-ups:

1. is_flags_reader now consults is_cond_jcc() — the authoritative
   mnemonic list — before the LineKind-based check. The classifier keys
   is_conditional_jump on the second character, so `jc` classifies as
   Other while `jnc` classifies as CondJmp; a post-branch reader of that
   spelling escaped the post-jcc guard and would have consumed the
   producer's flags after the rewrite (caught by the new
   setcc_fuse_refuses_jcc_reader_after_branch with a `jc` after the
   branch — the fusion emitted jne and changed the reader's condition).

2. The deadness scan now stops at any conditional-jump spelling
   (is_cond_jcc): the branch target may rejoin and read the carrier, so
   the provable dead window ends at the branch, not at the classifier's
   kind for it.

3. Red-team tests for the fusion: dead window (setCC..relay dropped,
   jcc rewritten onto the producer CC with identical branch polarity),
   je-inversion, movzwl/AH-garbage carrier refusal, post-branch jcc
   reader refusal (jc spelling), setCC reader behind the fallthrough
   label refusal, writer-before-reader allowance, and the live-bool
   window-kept shape. cmpl-headed producers make refusals observable
   (no other pass may drop a cmpl-headed setCC test) and make a wrong
   fusion's je->jne rewrite detectable.

4. mulacc differential tests (GCC-oracle): kstrtoull-shaped chains with
   overflow gates, sext/negative addend feeders, hi-zero boundary bases
   (0xFFFFFFFF) vs rejected >=2^32 bases, and the single-use no-op cast
   sandwich rule (multi-use casts must break the chain). All byte-exact
   vs GCC -O2 at every level, fusion on and off.

5. stmt_expr_asm_typeof returned 42 (the payload it asserts on) instead
   of 0; the runner's exit-0 protocol requires a real success code. Both
   lccc and GCC returned 42 — a test-expectation defect, not a codegen
   one.

Validation: unit 1258/0/6, regression corpus 516 total with the two
-m32 run-fails resolved as environment (missing i386 crt; binaries
were linked without crt1.o and crashed at the final ret — with
libc6-dev-i386 installed both exit 0), sqlite_varint miscompile
(pre-existing, under investigation) documented separately.
