Subject: [PATCH 2/3] x86: fix two pre-existing miscompiles surfaced by the
 corpus
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. MachInst two-address aliasing (sqlite_varint, benchmark corpus):

   The simple-ALU lowering emits `mov lhs,dst; alu rhs,dst`, which reads
   rhs AFTER dst is written. The register allocator only guarantees the
   IR's read-then-write semantics, so homing rhs and dest in one register
   is legal there — and the machine form silently computed `lhs OP lhs`.
   sqlite3GetVarint's `b <<= 14; b |= *p` hit exactly this: the byte load
   and the dest homed to %edx, the OR became `or %edx,%edx`, and every
   9-byte varint decoded wrong (check_known_values bailed, rc=2, no
   output). Lowering now enforces the machine constraint at ISel time:
   commutative ops (Add/And/Or/Xor/Mul) swap operands so the surviving
   source is the register-homed non-dest one; Sub and both-alias shapes
   fall back to the mature emitter (lower_binop now returns bool and the
   dispatcher honours it). Flags are not observable through IR BinOp, so
   the swap is transparent. Bisection path: MI_DISABLE_KINDS=binop /
   CCC_NO_MACHINST / CCC_NO_BLOCK_RELAYOUT / CCC_NO_LEAF_PARAM_GPR all
   masked it; the MI stream contained the OR, the final asm did not.

2. F128 intrinsic results (glibc_f128_builtins):

   Intrinsic::result_type() returned None for F128Fabs/F128Neg/
   F128Copysign, so the stack-slot allocator reserved 8 bytes for their
   destinations while the codegen stores 16 (movdqu). The store overwrote
   the adjacent slot: copysign's result temp at 0x18(%rsp) clobbered the
   operand's 16-byte slot at 0x20, corrupting the operand for every
   subsequent operation (the second copysign read a half-garbage x and
   produced high=low qword duplication). result_type() now reports F128
   for the three bit-op builtins, sizing their slots correctly. Reduced
   to three intrinsics off one operand + eq128 calls.

Validation: regression corpus 506/506 executable tests green (10
legitimate skip-compares where GCC cannot build its oracle), unit
1258/0/6, compat 20/20, boot gate PASS at _end=31168 with the flat
setup image byte-identical to the ld.bfd oracle.
